  "aiContextParagraph": "President Prabowo Subianto engaged in high-level bilateral and multilateral discussions during the APEC summit, resulting in potential investment commitments totaling Rp1,600 trillion for Indonesia. Alongside these economic outcomes, the summit served as a platform for significant geopolitical engagement between major world powers. Notably, a trilateral meeting involving Donald Trump, Xi Jinping, and Vladimir Putin became a focal point of analysis, with observers discussing their non-verbal cues and the difficulty of reaching consensus on global issues such as nuclear restrictions. The event also included criticism directed toward Donald Trump following his remarks about Vladimir Putin, and comments from NATO Secretary General Mark Rutte regarding international security concerns. President Vladimir Putin also formally acknowledged Indonesia's role during the proceedings, marking a period of intense diplomatic activity among the gathered heads of state and government representatives.",
